{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick","id":1478145,"title":"What is the most practical and impractical form of Pillar Magick ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-06T09:04:21-07:00","id":1478145,"title":"What is the most practical and impractical form of Pillar Magick ?","content":"There's 8 different types of pillar magic- <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pillar_(DAM)\" target=\"_blank\">Link to Pillars Page</a> &gt; Thank you <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\">HorizonParty2021</a> !</b><br /> <br /> You may need to copy and paste the link in a new tab.<br /> <br /> In my opinion the most practical of the pillar magicks would have to be the totems used by the Spirit-Talkers. The totems seem extremely versatile and seems to have the most bang for your buck. You really want to ruin someone's day? Summon a snowstorm! Plus you can even control ghosts! You want to freak someone out? Summon up their Ancestors! It just seems like a pretty cool power. Spirits themselves can encompass many different things as well, you want to read some ones mind? Just get a spirit to do that for you. It feels like that's something a spirit can do.<br /> <br /> Most impractical has to be the, Subversions of Divine Will used by the Circle of Red. Its extremely underwhelming, Dark thaumaturgy is 10x better.<br /> <br /> I may be wrong about all this so correct me if I am wrong.<br /> <br /> What in you opinion is the most practical and impractical form of Pillar Magick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 04-06-2022, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T09:16:52-07:00","id":1478148,"title":"","content":"As best deal in terms of power and versatility goes, I see a neck-to-neck race between Hermetic, Old Faith, and Messianic Voices, with Spirit Talkers being not too far behind.<br /> <br /> As for the most impractical set of Foundation and Pillars, I rank Circle of Red worst (these morons went to the Dark Side to get the crappiest set of Pillars? Talk about infernalists being suckers), Ahl-i-Batini second (too many common feats of magic are out of reach, esp. if you don't care to be an especially subtle kind of mage, and the High Magic Age is not exactly the best period for that) and Valdaermen third (the Pillars themselves are not too bad, although overall worse than the OoH, MV, OF and ST ones, but a Foundation based on suffering leaves much to be desired; the main selling point of the Fellowship is easy access to luck effects). In this period, Craftmasons are just OoH deviants with a less convenient paradigm and set of foci, and you can get Materia as a vanilla Hermetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-06-2022, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:"