":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478152#post1478152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pillar_(DAM)\" target=\"_blank\">Link to Pillars Page</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, forgot we could do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-06T19:37:17-07:00","id":1478181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478148#post1478148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As best deal in terms of power and versatility goes, I see a neck-to-neck race between Hermetic, Old Faith, and Messianic Voices, with Spirit Talkers being not too far behind.<br /> <br /> As for the most impractical set of Foundation and Pillars, I rank Circle of Red worst (these morons went to the Dark Side to get the crappiest set of Pillars? Talk about infernalists being suckers), Ahl-i-Batini second (too many common feats of magic are out of reach, esp. if you don't care to be an especially subtle kind of mage, and the High Magic Age is not exactly the best period for that) and Valdaermen third (the Pillars themselves are not too bad, although overall worse than the OoH, MV, OF and ST ones, but a Foundation based on suffering leaves much to be desired; the main selling point of the Fellowship is easy access to luck effects). In this period, Craftmasons are just OoH deviants with a less convenient paradigm and set of foci, and you can get Materia as a vanilla Hermetic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah dark tahumathurgy was way better than whatever the red circle had.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-07T11:07:40-07:00","id":1478224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478181#post1478181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah dark tahumathurgy was way better than whatever the red circle had.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you want to play or set up as NPC an Infernalist mage in DA:M that got something worthwhile from giving their allegiance to Hell, you'd better ignore the Circle of Red entirely and create a Thrall that kept the usual Foundation and Pillars from their Fellowships and combined them with appropriate Arcana. If you set things up the right way, you can get a character that combines Awakened magic (possibly boosted if made a little more risky with Infernal boons) with equal or better resilience to mundane damage and/or enhancement of physical abilities as vampires, mystical drawbacks of infernalism that are no worse than vampire, mage, or fae supernatural weaknesses, and a master-vassal relationship with a demon that already ended or is not especially abusive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T10:37:52-07:00","id":1478390,"title":"","content":"Eh, Circle of the Red was always more intended as an antagonist for Demon PC's. So it being not that great isn't surprising.<br /> <br /> As for most practical. Honestly, I'd say the Valdaermen by far and away are the most 'Practical' each of their pillars has practical applications, though in very different fields and are generally good enough to stand on their own as power sets. By comparison, the OoH has a rather cut down set of the traditional spheres. Whereas most of the others have some sort of blended power set as their pillars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T13:35:20-07:00","id":1478420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478390#post1478390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for most practical. Honestly, I'd say the Valdaermen by far and away are the most 'Practical' each of their pillars has practical applications, though in very different fields and are generally good enough to stand on their own as power sets. By comparison, the OoH has a rather cut down set of the traditional spheres. Whereas most of the others have some sort of blended power set as their pillars.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't deny that a few Valdaermen Pillars (Forlog and Hjaldar) cannot have some serious usefulness, although IMO the other two Pillars are subpar in comparison to OoH, MV, OF, or ST ones. However, Blot is rather more burdensome to develop and maintain than most other Foundations. According to DA:M Grimoire, you risk backsliding in the Foundation smply because your lifestyle gets too comfortable by Middle Ages standards, not to mention self-mutilation being the most preferred form of development. Thanks, but no thanks. I like having a spare of eyes and hands very much. <br /> <br /> The OoH Pillars are so great precisely because they are the practical equivalent of the most useful and versatile Spheres (including Materia from the Grimoire, you get all the Pattern Spheres plus Mind and Prime). I agree MV, OF, and ST Pillars mostly work as blended mixes of various Spheres, including all the most valuable ones, and this is what makes them great as well. <br /> <br /> Batini Pillars suck unless you are dead-set to be the super-subtle and manipulative kind of mage or a fate/space specialist. No thanks. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T14:20:36-07:00","id":1478428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478420#post1478420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Batini Pillars suck unless you are dead-set to be the super-subtle and manipulative kind of mage or a fate/space specialist. No thanks. </div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;suck&quot; I assume you mean &quot;absolute coolest and best kind of Mage conceivable.&quot; \ud83d\ude1c<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, the only thing the Batini are missing that would make their Pillar set perfect for my personal taste is a version of the Prime Sphere (maybe they have something, dunno, DAM is not something I'm very familiar with). <br /> <br /> Really, what is the most practical or impractical power-set is going to depend on your interests or goals. I should note that mastery of Mind verges on de facto master of anything that you can brainwash someone into doing for you, assuming you're a monster lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T14:40:21-07:00","id":1478429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478428#post1478428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By &quot;suck&quot; I assume you mean &quot;absolute coolest and best kind of Mage conceivable.&quot; \ud83d\ude1c<br /> <br /> In all seriousness, the only thing the Batini are missing that would make their Pillar set perfect for my personal taste is a version of the Prime Sphere (maybe they have something, dunno, DAM is not something I'm very familiar with).<br /> <br /> Really, what is the most practical or impractical power-set is going to depend on your interests or goals. I should note that mastery of Mind verges on de facto master of anything that you can brainwash someone into doing for you, assuming you're a monster lol</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, YMMV. My perspective is dead-set on cheering for flashy feats of magic and not giving subtle ones (unless they have to be so by their very nature, such as most Mind or Fate/Entropy ones) the time of day, and my judgement on what is or is not useful or practical shapes accordingly. I may point out that the Hermetics, Messianics, Old Faith, and Spirit Talkers have plenty of means in their own Pillars to do anything a Batini can do about Mind manipulation, as well as lots more with ease about various common uses of magic that a so-called Subtle One cannot easily do without going through rather convolute applications of their Pillars (see the relevant section of the Grimoire). Batini (or Valdaermen) magic is very good for space or fate manipulation, nothing more or nothing less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T15:15:28-07:00","id":1478433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478429#post1478429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sure, YMMV. My perspective is dead-set on cheering for flashy feats of magic and not giving subtle ones (unless they have to be so by their very nature, such as most Mind or Fate/Entropy ones) the time of day, and my judgement on what is or is not useful or practical shapes accordingly. I may point out that the Hermetics, Messianics, Old Faith, and Spirit Talkers have plenty of means in their own Pillars to do anything a Batini can do about Mind manipulation, as well as lots more with ease about various common uses of magic that a so-called Subtle One cannot easily do without going through rather convolute applications of their Pillars (see the relevant section of the Grimoire). Batini (or Valdaermen) magic is very good for space or fate manipulation, nothing more or nothing less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm less here to stan for the Batini and more to emphasize what you've basically already acknowledged; this is more a question of *perspective* than one you can realistically answer in a general and objective fashion. Whether or not being &quot;flashy&quot; is practical or impractical depends on what you hope to achieve. Being &quot;flashy&quot; can put a target on your back, and being less capable of achieving your goals through the magical equivalent of brute force may be more practical if you'd rather avoid people gunning for you as a comparatively obvious target.<br /> <br /> I would like to note that teleportation is one of the go-to examples of powerful magic. Acknowledging that I'm not an expert on DA Mage or Pillars, are there other groups that have access to spatial manipulation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T16:36:56-07:00","id":1478441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478433#post1478433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm less here to stan for the Batini and more to emphasize what you've basically already acknowledged; this is more a question of *perspective* than one you can realistically answer in a general and objective fashion</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, full agreement here. A necessary premise to this kind of analysis is deciding what one means to do with magic. Mine includes the ability to perform most kinds of common magic feats through the mystical equivalent of brute force with relative ease and safety. In my perspective, this a major and necessary component of 'true' or 'real' magic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whether or not being &quot;flashy&quot; is practical or impractical depends on what you hope to achieve. Being &quot;flashy&quot; can put a target on your back, and being less capable of achieving your goals through the magical equivalent of brute force may be more practical if you'd rather avoid people gunning for you as a comparatively obvious target. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the reward is totally worth the risk from my perspective. I may point out that being able to harness a great deal of brute force at need and use it easily and efficiently oftentimes is an excellent way to deal with the problem of potential hostiles. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would like to note that teleportation is one of the go-to examples of powerful magic. Acknowledging that I'm not an expert on DA Mage or Pillars, are there other groups that have access to spatial manipulation? </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the Batini and the Valdaermen have Pillars that are specialized for travel or space manipulation and hence well suited for this kind of feat. The other Fellowships nowhere so much, although they may often access other means of quick and efficient travel, such as flight, shapeshifting, and/or weather control. Also please notice that traveling to the Umbra (and possibly using it as a means of quick travel) is a wholly different matter, and the other Fellowships often are proficient in it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-09T22:24:24-07:00","id":1478470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478441#post1478441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, full agreement here. A necessary premise to this kind of analysis is deciding what one means to do with magic. Mine includes the ability to perform most kinds of common magic feats through the mystical equivalent of brute force with relative ease and safety. In my perspective, this a major and necessary component of 'true' or 'real' magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, one's perspective is one's perspective, but setting that kind of bar for magic to qualify as &quot;real&quot; or &quot;true&quot; is the one thing you've said here that I'm strongly inclined to disagree with. Magic is magic because it's magic, which is to say that whatever you are doing is achieved by paranormal/supernatural power, rather than obeying the laws of science as we understand them. How powerful or impressive the result isn't really what matters, but rather the method of attaining the result. Maybe it just comes from the shallow look I've taken at the subject of chaos magic, specifically the idea of magic as the ability to induce synchronicities, events that appear as mere coincidence but can be linked with the perception or will of the practitioner, but I've become less interested in &quot;magic&quot; as &quot;a flashy way to blow stuff up&quot; in recent years.<br /> <br /> You are of course free to prefer whatever type of magic you wish, but to try and set a definition for what qualifies as &quot;real&quot; or &quot;true&quot; seems to move beyond a statement of opinion or perspective, into a matter of fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478441#post1478441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but the reward is totally worth the risk from my perspective. I may point out that being able to harness a great deal of brute force at need and use it easily and efficiently oftentimes is an excellent way to deal with the problem of potential hostiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with &quot;The Order of the Stick,&quot; specifically the prequel comic &quot;Start of Darkness&quot;? It includes a page that really demonstrates this point in quite an entertaining fashion (alas I don't think I can find a copy floating around the internet). It is indeed a very functional solution in many cases, though subtlety and technique can be equally effective IMO. I must admit, as much as I admire subtlety, I often tend to resort to more brute-force solutions myself in practice, haha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478441#post1478441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, the Batini and the Valdaermen have Pillars that are specialized for travel or space manipulation and hence well suited for this kind of feat. The other Fellowships nowhere so much, although they may often access other means of quick and efficient travel, such as flight, shapeshifting, and/or weather control. Also please notice that traveling to the Umbra (and possibly using it as a means of quick travel) is a wholly different matter, and the other Fellowships often are proficient in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I took a bit of time to look at the Valdaermen Runes, and I must admit they are rather impressive. They manage to mirror a lot of the more interesting and useful effects you can find among the Batini Pillars, while also including some of the abilities from Prime and Spirit that I really like as well. Which did remind me that, aside from the already mentioned lack of Prime abilities, the Batini not having any talent for accessing the Umbra is probably their other big shortcoming from my perspective. But Mind, Prime, Correspondence, and Time are probably my favourite Spheres, while Spirit is really cool but not quite one of my favourites despite its considerable utility. Given the opportunity I would of course want my character to be skilled at all types of magic, but that's not really feasible until you're getting into Master/Archmage territory, and until then you've got to choose priorities.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'll take another look at your topic about Dual Affiliations in DA Mage and consider which pairing might give me all my favourite toys lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-10T04:52:11-07:00","id":1478479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1478145-what-is-the-most-practical-and-impractical-form-of-pillar-magick?p=1478470#post1478470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, one's perspective is one's perspective, but setting that kind of bar for magic to qualify as &quot;real&quot; or &quot;true&quot; is the one thing you've said here that I'm strongly inclined to disagree with. Magic is magic because it's magic, which is to say that whatever you are doing is achieved by paranormal/supernatural power, rather than obeying the laws of science as we understand them. How powerful or impressive the result isn't really what matters, but rather the method of attaining the result. Maybe it just comes from the shallow look I've taken at the subject of chaos magic, specifically the idea of magic as the ability to induce synchronicities, events that appear as mere coincidence but can be linked with the perception or will of the practitioner, but I've become less interested in &quot;magic&quot; as &quot;a flashy way to blow stuff up&quot; in recent years.<br /> <br /> You are of course free to prefer whatever type of magic you wish, but to try and set a definition for what qualifies as &quot;real&quot; or &quot;true&quot; seems to move beyond a statement of opinion or perspective, into a matter of fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I do not mean to dismiss or demean the validity of perspectives like yours. If subtlety and apparent coincidence work for you, they work, and good for you. I am happy things work well for you that way on your end. My description of brute-force magic being the only 'true' or 'real' kind for me is simply an attempt to describe how things register to me. I feel happy and fulfilled being able to do things this way, annoyed and frustrated having to do them the other way. The main exception is when an effect is subtle by its very nature or really works best that way, such as mental manipulation or fate/luck spells.<br /> <br /> I suppose it is no coincidence (heh) that two of my three most preferred Spheres (Forces, Life, and Mind), besides being some of the most powerful and versatile ones, are also among the ones that often work best this way. Mind is just as powerful and versatile but Exhibit A for the 'subtle by nature' exception. Entropy is usually next in the priority scale but a mixed bag for me. I fancy the direct death/destruction effects, and I find the fate/luck ones often rewarding and useful for personal benefits but not my preferred solution to problems if a simpler brute-force one exists. If it doesn't, the exception applies. As it concerns the necromancy stuff, either it is useful as a tool for immortality, or Spirit is usually a more versatile alternative, or it does not interest me. Correspondence, Prime, Matter, and Spirit are often useful in their niches but not my preferred solution if an alternative exists. MtA often makes Prime practically necessary to some serious degree, but the situation is more complex for DA. I have little overall use for Time, except as a tool for immortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It includes a page that really demonstrates this point in quite an entertaining fashion (alas I don't think I can find a copy floating around the internet). It is indeed a very functional solution in many cases, though subtlety and technique can be equally effective IMO. I must admit, as much as I admire subtlety, I often tend to resort to more brute-force solutions myself in practice, haha. </div> </div> </div>Sure. As I said, I find subtlety occasionally acceptable or useful when it is the natural way of doing things or the by far most convenient method, but I have little patience with it when a brute-force solution seems available and just as or even more effective. I tend to find manipulation a tiresome way of dealing with problems, and straightforward brute-force solutions more rewarding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I took a bit of time to look at the Valdaermen Runes, and I must admit they are rather impressive. They manage to mirror a lot of the more interesting and useful effects you can find among the Batini Pillars, while also including some of the abilities from Prime and Spirit that I really like as well. </div> </div> </div>I won't deny the Valdaermen package has its selling points. My biggest gripe with it is the Foundation requirements, IMO one of the most inconvenient ones among the Fellowships, at least if you care for your ability to keep your body intact and have a decent lifestyle. I greatly appreciate the ability to withstand unavoidable hardship but denial or sacrifice for their own sake or even as a preferential way of (supposed) self-improvement register as off-putting and incomprehensible to me. Oddily enough, despite the Middle Ages having been the peak for often outlandish degrees of Christian ascetism, the Messianic Voices do not find themselves as burdened as the Valdaermen with too many explict requirements for sacrifice. I suppose it happens because to a large degree they are able to replace that with personal submission and abasement to their idea of the divine, which I find just as off-putting (also because the Middle Ages Christianity idea of God typically registers to me as the biggest tyrant and monster of them all).<br /> <br /> As a rule, another preference of mine about magic and mysticism is strong sympathy for the Left-Hand Path. In Mage paradigm terms, it typically plots to a mix of Order of Hermes (without unnecessary ritual), Verbena (without unnecessary sacrifice), Cult of Ecstasy (without hippie pacifism), and Taftani (the scorn for subtlety). In DA terms, it usually means OoH, Old Faith, or their mix.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe I'll take another look at your topic about Dual Affiliations in DA Mage and consider which pairing might give me all my favourite toys lol. </div> </div> </div>Please do. You have my blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 04-10-2022, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}